WEBVTT

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:05.270
I'm the unfortunate man who's been tasked 
with your education, Robert Capa.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.100
The job of a shooter class holder 
is to snipe enemies at range.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.240
You may be an E-gene holder,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.420
but in using your body to fight an enemy,
 you're no different from a common soldier.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.390
The commander has high hopes for you.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.210
I'm Harold S. Conway, 
2nd Lt. in the U.S. Air Force.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.740
If it's not a bother, we'd love to have 
a meal with you sometime.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:32.410
E-gene holders are the only ones who can 
beat the Evolutionary Invasion Objects,

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.700
so have more confidence!

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.610
You didn't come here 
to make friends.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:43.450
Take your anger at screwing up 
in Taiwan out on yourself.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.650
If you take them lightly 'cause they're copies,
 you'll get yourself killed.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.670
Predict the enemy's movements.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:51.890
Ah, I went ahead and took 
them with your copies.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.650
<b>Not her real boob</b>

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:51.650
<b>'shopped?</b>

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:52.650
Ugh!

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.450
Nice shots, don't you think?

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.560
The radar's picked up something!

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.360
Is this a...?!

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.870
It appears that D-101 was shot down 
while observing the hurricane.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.650
No... No way...

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:13.100
Abilities of distinguished individuals, 
numerous throughout history,

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.380
have been stored in special E-genes.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:15.380
<b>E-genes</b>

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:19.000
The E-gene holders, 
who inherit those genes,

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.760
<b>AU balls</b>

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:24.720
summon the abilities sleeping 
within them via AU balls,

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.400
and embody AU weapons.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:34.130
The E-gene holders belonging to the 
supranational organization Dogoo

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:37.100
versus enemies from outer space 
known as Evolutionary Invasion Objects.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.670
This is the chronicle of their 
fateful battle for humanity!

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.530
Gun No. 4: Hurricane!

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.340
<b>Special Duty Ship C. F.</b>

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.360
<b>CH-53 E. S.</b>

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:28.470
Hurricane Olga is currently 
approaching Florida.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:34.350
Our satellite took this image, 
and we magnified it.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.300
This is...

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:40.650
Upon analyzing the report from D-101,

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.280
we've determined that this shadow 
is an Invasion Object.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:48.250
Did we hear anything from the 
Hurricane Hunters after that?

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.550
We haven't been able to make 
contact since then.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:54.520
If it's not the Bermuda Triangle 
curse, then...

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:57.280
That thing got them.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:08.410
The Invasion Object intends to ride the 
hurricane to penetrate inland directly.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.740
Did they come up with that when they 
were beaten on the shore in Taiwan?

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.130
It's certainly a unique way 
to make a landing.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:19.630
We don't have time to be fascinated.

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:24.570
On top of being protected by 
a wall of 60 m/s winds,

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:28.820
it's riding the wind itself, 
and is moving at high speed.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.710
It'd be impossible to engage for a fight.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:37.350
Aside from shooting it down at range, 
there's no way to stop it from reaching land.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.280
You're going to have Ogura Sio do that?

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:44.340
How is she coming along, Mister Amash?

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:48.250
If you mean skills, yeah, she has them.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:52.600
But if she can't beat an opponent who's 
been declared unfit for battle,

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.070
there's no way she's ready.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:58.690
I see. So we'll need to get 
a different holder to...

00:04:58.930 --> 00:04:59.820
No.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:04.740
We need a shooter class holder 
this time, no matter what.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.680
Since William Tell is engaged 
with another Object...

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:11.340
Nobunagun.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.010
She's all we have.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:24.380
Am I really gonna be okay 
sortieing all of a sudden?

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.160
Wah! Uh! Er!

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:36.810
<b>Oh, she definitely sees it. </b>

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:41.510
You've gotta be the most brazen 
peeper I've ever seen.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:46.580
B-But I wasn't, not-even-in-the-
slightest-least-bit, trying to peep!

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:46.580
Simmer down and get changed! 

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.780
<b>High school girl voyeur </b>

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:47.960
Okay...

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:55.760
Jack, you're all healed up now, right?

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:59.010
Of course. How about you?

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:04.400
It sounds like Capa's training hasn't 
exactly produced results yet.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:09.420
Our accurate knowledge of the route 
this hurricane will travel

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:13.740
is all that's left to us in exchange 
for the lives of the Hurricane Hunters.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.070
So I'm gonna—

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:18.790
I'm not expecting anything from you.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:22.230
Wh— Whaaaa?!

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.200
Just don't get in my way.

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:29.230
What the hell?!

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.650
What's up with these E-gene holders, 
anyway?! Buncha weirdos!

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.370
<b>High school girl military otaku </b>

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:39.200
Could it really be that I'm the 
only normal E-gene holder?!

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:37.830
<b>Normal? </b>

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.200
And what the heck! 
How do you put this thing on?!

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.640
What're you doing?! 
Get yer ass on board!

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:56.940
Yessir!

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:02.820
Hurricane Olga, with a pressure 
center of 915 hPa.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.070
60 m/s winds.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:08.500
A storm zone with a radius of 180 km.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:13.220
It's a true fortress of wind, 
and that thing is inside.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:18.000
It's taken the wind under its pectoral fins, 
and is flying at high speeds inside the storm.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:23.040
It must be aiming to ride in on the 
hurricane and invade the mainland.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:28.820
We want to attack over water, 
but the peninsula of Florida is right there.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:31.380
On top of that, the helicopter 
can't get any closer than this.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:35.550
So we'll snipe the enemy inside 
the hurricane from here.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:38.780
Dispatch orders as follows:

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.430
The spotter is Galileo. {TB: Looked up this term, so it should be accurate.}

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:41.940
Yessir!

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.390
Oh! It talked!

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.930
You haven't been introduced yet, huh.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.050
This is Galileo.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.820
N-Nice to meet you.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.210
<b>Dear Mom, All E-gene holders are weirdos.</b>

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.960
Galileo, what's the position of 
the Invasion Object?

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.960
I've got it in my sight, 
so we're good to go.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:06.100
The enemy will pass by in 
approximately 90 seconds.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:08.410
Take a good look.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:11.680
You're the sniper, Nobunagun.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:23.250
Here it comes!

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:37.440
It's huge! Anyone should be 
able to hit that thing...

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:40.170
...even a half-trained squirt like you.

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:46.460
Yeah. No matter where we hit it, 
it'll probably fall into the ocean.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.880
Jack the Ripper, you'll deliver the 
final blow to the fallen target.

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:51.420
Aye, aye.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:54.330
Even a guy who just healed 
up a big hole in his belly

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:56.880
should be able to handle that, right?

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.100
What?!

00:08:58.570 --> 00:08:59.760
What?!

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:00.740
What?

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.070
What!!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.040
When I analyzed the video 
of it passing by just now,

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:08.000
I found it to be carrying a 
large number of eggs.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:09.480
What?!

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.160
That's...

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.940
Huh? Huh? What's that mean?

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:18.170
It means its aim is to scatter 
the eggs over the ground...

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:20.980
in order to spawn a species 
that can live on land.

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:26.760
If it takes a hit from us, it'll drop 
those eggs without waiting for landfall.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:31.960
They'd be a problem even dropped in the ocean, 
but at this distance, some will make it to land.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:35.510
At that point, it'll be a 
hurricane disaster zone.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:39.710
We won't be able to get in there and 
destroy them all before they hatch.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.550
In other words...

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:48.990
In other words, we have to kill it in one shot, 
leaving no time for it to scatter eggs.

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:51.500
At this distance! At this relative velocity!

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.750
With your skill!

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:57.040
HQ!

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.280
We were listening.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:02.280
If the results from dissecting the Palau 
Invasion Object are any indication,

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:06.090
the organ equivalent to the 
brain in one with five eyes...

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:08.260
...is between the two eyes 
in the back row.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.120
So set your sight on that pinpoint.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.340
Oh no-no-no-no-no-no-no!

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.260
I-can't-I-can't-I-can't-I-can't!

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:17.770
As I thought, perhaps a 
change to the plan...

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:22.770
That won't do. Ogura Sio— 
no, Nobunagun.

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:27.390
This is something only you can do.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:31.970
Okay.

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:37.130
Relative velocity confirmed! The target 
will be nearest us in 240 seconds!

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:39.410
Everyone to your battle stations!

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:58.700
Miss Nobunagun, I'm sending 
my visuals to your scope.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.110
I'm adjusting for wind and 
atmospheric pressure,

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:04.690
so the bullet will fly straight 
for the center.

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.850
If I... If I don't hit it...

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:11.850
If I can't do this, like back then,

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.110
those things'll make it to land again!

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:17.480
Calm down!

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:19.490
Remember your training!

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:22.000
Don't panic! Reign in the power!

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:25.030
Rather than power, concentrate 
on accuracy!

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:29.810
Ugh, stop nagging!

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:33.070
Here it comes! It'll be nearest 
in 120 seconds!

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:40.730
Everything's swaying... That thing is, 
the helicopter is...

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.290
I gotta hit it.

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:49.420
I gotta hit it! I gotta hit it! 
I gotta hit it! I gotta hit it!

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.540
Like we thought...

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:56.820
She can't do it.

00:11:58.770 --> 00:12:01.350
Miss Nobunagun, just stay calm.

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:06.450
My lord, please calm yourself.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:11.190
The Imagawa army has 50,000 men. 
We have just over 2,000.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:13.480
It's too reckless to take the offensive!

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:17.940
I think it advisable to gather our men 
and barricade ourselves in this castle.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.100
My lord!

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:23.440
Did you find them?

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:28.440
Yes, the Imagawas transported 
provisions to Odaka Castle.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:34.300
So Yoshimoto is going from 
Kutsukake to Odaka...

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:36.490
Bring my drum!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.400
"A human's life is just 50 years... {TB: This bit is a quote from a Noh play, "Atsumori," but I couldn't find the one from actual published translation. in time.}

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:55.140
Compared to all that exists 
under the heavens...

00:12:55.140 --> 00:13:00.330
...it is but dreams and illusion."

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:02.710
Wh— What's going on?

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:04.920
She's dancing?

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:13.180
"Once given life...

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:21.530
...there is nothing which does not perish."

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:23.320
We take the offensive!

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:24.320
Huh?

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.250
The wind, the wind, the wind!

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:40.460
We can chase the wind in this baby.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:43.030
If I can catch the wind...!

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:45.880
The same wind!

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.190
She jumped out.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.380
Yeah, we just saw.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.550
That idiot. What is she thinking?!

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:06.770
Nobunagun has jumped out 
of the helicopter.

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:10.460
Invasion Object is approaching rapidly! 
Contact in 20 seconds.

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:13.240
19, 18, 17...

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:15.780
If I can ride the same 
wind as that thing...

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:17.920
Whoa, that was close!

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:18.480
There!

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:27.630
We're swaying... together now! Right on!

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:30.290
Smack between the eyes!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.480
Shit, can't see a thing!

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.460
Galileo!

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:41.260
The bullet Nobunagun fired 
made a direct hit!

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:42.860
All right!

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.250
What? What the—?!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.890
This is... not good!

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:52.230
What's wrong?

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:54.550
It didn't work! The Invasion 
Object is unharmed!

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:57.280
Whadaya mean? She shot straight 
through its head, didn't she?

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:59.640
Yes, the snipe was successful.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:02.020
But that head was just a transporter.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:05.170
The part carrying the eggs is separate.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:11.000
In other words, that Invasion Object 
was two joined together!

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.450
But that's...

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:15.010
Invasion Objects that join together...?

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:18.940
Invasion Object 1 is down! 
The split-off Invasion Object 2 is...

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:21.020
I-It's releasing eggs!

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.110
It's dropping the eggs!

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.020
I'll shoot it down.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.080
Wait! You'll never be able to!

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.450
Never mind the eggs, take out 
the Invasion Object!

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:33.090
Don't let it drop any more eggs!

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:34.560
Roger!

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.330
Smack between the eyes!

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:40.480
What's wrong?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:43.580
That sucker-like thing on 
its head is solid.

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:45.950
I've got no choice.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:57.640
The brain! I have to shoot through its brain!

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.650
It's gonna drop more eggs!

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.680
Outta the way, Squirt!

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:07.640
All we gotta do is cut its head off.

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:09.490
Okay!

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.070
Jack the Ripper has defeated 
Invasion Object 2!

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:16.300
Hey, could you please use 
your own parachute?!

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:18.680
We'll need mine later.

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:19.920
Galileo!

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:21.590
Y-Yessir!

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.600
How many eggs went flying?

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:25.900
Twelve!

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:28.510
All right, we're goin' after 'em.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:29.550
What?!

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:38.130
Let's go! I'm gonna smash all the eggs 
before they reach the ground!

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:39.670
And you're gonna help!

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:44.990
But I... I dunno if I can hit 
a target that size...

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:47.510
But...I guess I just have to, huh.

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:48.170
Dumbass!

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.080
What?!

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:52.430
I said you're gonna <i>help</i>. 
<i>I'm</i> gonna smash 'em.

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:54.360
So what am I doing, then?

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:57.470
Time to bust out the Three-Line 
Volley, Nobunagun!

00:16:58.450 --> 00:16:59.900
Whaaaaat?!

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:01.730
Wait a—! What? What?

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:05.420
Listen up, I'm not gonna be a 
tightwad like Capa.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:07.190
Gimme full power.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:10.960
Use your strength to carry me!

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:12.300
Carry?

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.710
Propel me after those eggs!

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:17.200
Uh— oh! Got it!

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:26.180
180 meters to the first egg! At 2'4'0'!

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.700
There it is. A little to the left!

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:33.990
That's one down!

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:35.710
Okay, on to the next!

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:36.540
Right!

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:41.790
At 6'3'3'! Just under 200 meters away!

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:48.790
Amazing! Fifth one destroyed!

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:51.180
Oh, sixth one! And another!

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:53.270
They're flying using the 
gun's power...?

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:54.460
Crazy...

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:57.890
Those two are performing well, huh.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:01.780
Oh no!

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:11.430
Miss Nobunagun! Mr. Jack!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:15.950
We've got an Object!

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:18.780
Yeah! An' it's gonna be hurting soon.

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:37.430
All Invasion Objects destroyed!

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.360
We beat 'em...?

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:46.490
Yeah, every last one.

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.220
Phew...

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:52.900
Hey! Now's not the time 
to be fallin' asleep!

00:18:57.430 --> 00:18:58.730
Jeezus.

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:07.280
There they are!

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:12.190
Mr. Jack, Miss Nobunagun, 
are you all right?

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.650
No, no we're not.

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:18.150
We've recovered Jack the Ripper 
and Nobunagun.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:20.760
And the defeated Invasion Object?

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:22.190
We're sending out a search party.

00:19:24.610 --> 00:19:26.240
Is something wrong?

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:29.460
No, the sea off Florida is probably fine now.

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:31.810
But there is something else on my mind.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:36.500
Yes. This time the Invasion Object 
came from the Atlantic Ocean.

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:39.600
Could it be that an enemy broke 
through at Panama?

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:41.530
Or...

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:43.500
It's possible, but...

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:47.900
I was thinking about what Capa was saying.

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:52.930
"Did they come up with that when they 
were beaten on the shore in Taiwan?"

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:57.180
Their first phase objective 
is to make landfall.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:19:59.740
The first time they managed that was Taiwan,

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:04.860
but before the invasion could grow legs,

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:06.600
we stopped it.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:11.630
Then this time, as if to 
avoid a shore battle,

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:14.320
they tried to go directly inland 
by riding a hurricane.

00:20:15.870 --> 00:20:17.930
They're definitely learning.

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:22.110
But, how does an Object in Florida 
know about a defeat in Taiwan?

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:29.460
Up until now I thought they were scattered, 
evolving independently...

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:32.240
...but there is something 
transmitting information.

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:35.990
And a "brain" making strategic decisions.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:46.390
What are you jerks laughin' about?

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:49.070
It's not what you think!

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:59.560
Man, what a pain in the ass!

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:05.990
<i>Was funhnnn... hee hee...</i>

00:21:13.550 --> 00:21:14.650
Huh?

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:22.360
It's already... night?

00:21:26.730 --> 00:21:30.390
Dear Asao... 
So much stuff happened today!

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:35.790
I trained, sortied for the first 
time, beat the enemy...

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:39.810
And then...

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:48.430
There's so much stuff I wanna 
talk to you about!!!

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:53.010
Ughghgh there's no way!

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:54.970
Asaooooo!

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:29.040
Been awhile since seeing 
Nobunagun! Right, Newton?

00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:30.600
That's right, Gandhi.

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:31.810
Wha?! Wait a minute!

00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:36.030
Next time! Gun No. Five: 
"The Second Platoon."

00:23:36.840 --> 00:23:39.760
Sio, look forward to it!
